1
00:07:33,750 --> 00:07:39,750
A love story so unusual it has to be true.

2
00:15:07,500 --> 00:15:13,500
Carrington is a history, drama, romance film directed by Christopher Hampton.

3
00:22:41,250 --> 00:22:47,250
Painter Dora Carrington develops an intimate but extremely
complex bond with writer Lytton Strachey.

4
00:30:15,000 --> 00:30:21,000
Though Lytton is a homosexual, he is enchanted by the mysterious Dora and they
begin a lifelong friendship that has strangely romantic undertones.

5
00:37:48,750 --> 00:37:54,750
Eventually, Lytton and Dora decide to live together, despite the fact that the latter has
fallen in love with military man Ralph Partridge, whom she plans to marry.

6
00:45:22,500 --> 00:45:28,500
Dora Carrington, played by Emma Thompson.

7
00:52:56,250 --> 00:53:02,250
Lytton Strachey, played by Jonathan Pryce.

8
01:00:30,000 --> 01:00:36,000
Ralph Partridge, played by Steven Waddington.

9
01:08:03,750 --> 01:08:09,750
Gerald Brenan, played by Samuel West.

10
01:15:37,500 --> 01:15:43,500
Mark Gertler, played by Rufus Sewell.

11
01:23:11,250 --> 01:23:17,250
Lady Ottoline Morrell, played by Penelope Wilton.

12
01:30:45,000 --> 01:30:51,000
Carrington is a 1995 British biographical film written and directed by Christopher Hampton about the life
of the English painter Dora Carrington (1893–1932), who was known simply as "Carrington".

13
01:38:18,750 --> 01:38:24,750
The screenplay is based on Lytton Strachey: A Critical Biography, the 1967–68 two-volume
biography of writer and critic Lytton Strachey (1880–1932) by Michael Holroyd.

14
01:45:52,500 --> 01:45:58,500
The film explores themes of england, painter,
conscientious objector, soldier, polyamory.

15
01:53:26,250 --> 01:53:32,250
The tone is emotional and thought_provoking.
